# Cloud Build source-upload excludes (used by `gcloud builds submit ../..`).
# The image is built in-cluster — the Dockerfile runs the install + build — so
# dependencies, build outputs, and local tooling never need uploading. Keeping
# the tarball small also avoids the 300s upload timeout on slower links.
#
# NOTE: once this file exists, gcloud uses ONLY it (it no longer falls back to
# .gitignore), so this must list everything to exclude — including the nested
# .terraform dirs that .gitignore handles but the gcloud fallback missed.

.git/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Terraform working dirs: provider plugins are ~100+ MB and are never needed to
# build the app image (this is what was bloating the upload to ~188 MB).
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
terraform.tfvars
crash.log
